352b7d86ab83b82b1d35ab864f8acaf730c0e17","commits":[],"cumulative_patch_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855","finding_commits":{},"parent":"c352b7d86ab83b82b1d35ab864f8acaf730c0e17","patch_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855","tree":"8dc3a7b8561e409f33a7fedac3022178b15c6c2d"},"dispositions":{"comments":[{"body":"Failed handoffs lose transfer metadata that is already known. Both attributes are assigned only after `original_invoke` returns: an SDK `on_handoff` callback that raises produces an ERROR tool span containing neither attribute, although `selected.handoff.agent_name` already identifies `agent-b` and the mode is necessarily `pass_control`. This contradicts the new requirements in `model/gen-ai/spans.yaml:911-914`, which explicitly include failed attempts. Set the known mode and configured target when starting the span, then update the target after success if necessary, and add a failure-path test. The ADK wrapper at `reference/scenarios/google-adk/scenario.py:607-611` likewise drops the known mode when transfer argument validation fails.","line":405,"path":"reference/scenarios/openai-agents/scenario.py","side":"RIGHT"},{"body":"ADK validation failures are recorded as successful tool results. `TransferToAgentTool` inherits `FunctionTool.run_async`, which returns an `{'error': ...}` response for missing or invalid arguments rather than raising. A transfer call with arguments `{}` therefore leaves this span UNSET with no `error.type` and records the error payload in `gen_ai.tool.call.result`, despite that attribute's success-only contract. Inspect the SDK's `_detect_error_in_response(result)` hook (which reports `TOOL_ERROR`), set `error.type` and ERROR status on failure, and record the result only on success, following the existing skill wrapper at lines 767-772. Add a failed-transfer regression test.","line":612,"path":"reference/scenarios/google-adk/scenario.py","side":"RIGHT"}],"input